# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <MyComponent v-text="content" />
  <MyComponent v-html="html" />
  <MyComponent v-text="content"></MyComponent>
  <my-component v-html="html"></my-component>
  <router-link v-text="content" />
  <UI.Button v-text="content" />
  <component :is="component" v-text="content" />
  <component :is="component" v-html="html" />
  <component v-text="content" />
  <unknownelement v-text="content"></unknownelement>
  <Transition v-html="html"></Transition>
  <keep-alive v-text="content"></keep-alive>
  <tr is="vue:my-row" v-text="content"></tr>
  <div>
    <MyComponent v-if="visible" v-html="html" />
  </div>
  <svg><MyIcon v-text="content" /></svg>
</template>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.vue:3:16 lint/nursery/noVueVTextVHtmlOnComponent ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The v-text directive is used on a component.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │   <MyComponent v-text="content" />
      │                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    4 │   <MyComponent v-html="html" />
    5 │   <MyComponent v-text="content"></MyComponent>
  
  i Vue doesn't put the value in the component's slot. It replaces everything inside the component's root element, so the component's own content is lost.
  
  i Put the content between the component's opening and closing tags, or move v-text to an HTML element inside them.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

